[CENTER][IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Benoit-V/DiscordRankSync/master/docs/spigot/banner.png[/IMG]

[SIZE=5][B]Turn your in-game ranks into Discord roles — automatically.[/B][/SIZE]
Players link their Minecraft and Discord accounts in seconds, and their roles and nickname stay in sync on every join.
[B]Spigot / Paper • BungeeCord • Velocity[/B]

[URL='https://github.com/Benoit-V/DiscordRankSync']Source code[/URL]  •  [URL='https://bebedlastreat.fr/discord']Support Discord[/URL][/CENTER]

[IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Benoit-V/DiscordRankSync/master/docs/spigot/header-features.png[/IMG]
[IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Benoit-V/DiscordRankSync/master/docs/spigot/features.png[/IMG]

[LIST]
[*][B]Rank → role sync[/B]: every configured Discord role follows a permission (works with LuckPerms or any permission plugin). Roles are added and removed on each join.
[*][B]Nickname sync[/B]: linked members are renamed to their Minecraft name on Discord.
[*][B]Link rewards[/B]: run console commands when a player links (only on the very first link, or every time).
[*][B]Booster rewards[/B]: server boosters claim a reward in game with [I]/claimboost[/I], once a month or every X days.
[*][B]Clean unlinking[/B]: roles are removed on unlink, unlink commands are run, and members who leave the Discord server can be unlinked automatically.
[*][B]PlaceholderAPI[/B] support on your Spigot servers, even behind a proxy.
[*][B]Storage[/B]: SQLite (zero setup), MySQL / MariaDB or MongoDB.
[*][B]Networks[/B]: run it on your proxy, share data with your backends through plugin messages or Redis, and use several proxies with RedisBungee.
[*]Fully customizable messages with [URL='https://docs.advntr.dev/minimessage/format.html']MiniMessage[/URL] (gradients, colors…).
[/LIST]

[IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Benoit-V/DiscordRankSync/master/docs/spigot/header-how.png[/IMG]
[IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Benoit-V/DiscordRankSync/master/docs/spigot/how-it-works.png[/IMG]

[LIST=1]
[*]While connected to the Minecraft server, the player runs [I]/link <minecraft name>[/I] on Discord.
[*]The bot privately sends a 6-digit code. The player types [I]/link <code>[/I] in game within 5 minutes.
[*]The accounts are linked: link rewards run, the nickname is updated, and the roles are given the next time the player joins.
[/LIST]

[IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Benoit-V/DiscordRankSync/master/docs/spigot/header-setup.png[/IMG]

[LIST=1]
[*]Go to the [URL='https://discord.com/developers/applications']Discord Developer Portal[/URL] and create a new application.
[*]In the [B]Bot[/B] section, copy the token (you may have to reset it) and [B]enable the Server Members Intent[/B].
[*]Invite the bot to your server with the [I]bot[/I] and [I]applications.commands[/I] scopes and the [B]Manage Roles[/B] and [B]Manage Nicknames[/B] permissions.
[*][B]Move the bot's role above every role it has to give[/B] in your server settings. Discord does not let a bot give a role above its own.
[*]Put the jar in your [I]plugins[/I] folder (on your proxy if you have a network) and start the server once to generate [I]config.yml[/I].
[*]Fill in [I]bot-token[/I], [I]guild-id[/I] (right-click your server with Developer Mode enabled → Copy Server ID) and your [I]ranks[/I], then restart.
[/LIST]

[SPOILER="Minimal configuration example"]
[CODE=YAML]bot-token: "your-bot-token"
guild-id: "123456789012345678"
rename: true

ranks:
  vip:
    id: "234567890123456789"      # Discord role id
    permission: "group.vip"       # permission the player needs in game
  member:
    id: "345678901234567890"
    permission: "group.default"

database: "SQLite"                # SQLite, MySQL/MariaDB or MongoDB

one-time-reward: true
reward-command: ["eco give {player} 500"]
boost-reward: ["crate key give {player} booster 1"][/CODE]
[/SPOILER]

[IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Benoit-V/DiscordRankSync/master/docs/spigot/header-commands.png[/IMG]

[B]Discord (slash commands)[/B]
[LIST]
[*][I]/link <minecraft name>[/I] — start linking your Minecraft account (you must be online)
[*][I]/unlink[/I] — unlink your Minecraft account
[*][I]/minecraft <@user>[/I] — get the Minecraft account linked to a Discord user [COLOR=#808080](admins only by default)[/COLOR]
[*][I]/discord <minecraft name>[/I] — get the Discord account linked to a Minecraft player [COLOR=#808080](admins only by default)[/COLOR]
[*][I]/ping[/I] — show the bot latency
[/LIST]
[COLOR=#808080]Who can use the admin commands can be changed in your Discord server settings → Integrations.[/COLOR]

[B]Minecraft[/B]
[LIST]
[*][I]/link <code>[/I] — confirm the link with the code received on Discord
[*][I]/unlink[/I] — unlink your Discord account
[*][I]/claimboost[/I] — claim your reward if you boost the Discord server
[*][I]/stopbot[/I] (alias [I]/stopdiscord[/I]) — stop the Discord bot — permission [I]discord.stopbot[/I]
[/LIST]

[IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Benoit-V/DiscordRankSync/master/docs/spigot/header-placeholders.png[/IMG]

[LIST]
[*][I]%discordranksync_discord%[/I] — Discord name of the player (server nickname)
[*][I]%discordranksync_is_linked%[/I] — [I]true[/I] or [I]false[/I]
[*][I]%discordranksync_is_boost%[/I] — [I]true[/I] if the player boosts the Discord server
[*][I]%discordranksync_members%[/I] — number of members on the Discord server [COLOR=#808080](not available in standalone mode)[/COLOR]
[/LIST]
[COLOR=#808080]For players who are not linked, [I]discord[/I] and [I]is_boost[/I] return the [I]papi-not-linked[/I] message from the config.[/COLOR]

[IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Benoit-V/DiscordRankSync/master/docs/spigot/header-network.png[/IMG]

[LIST]
[*][B]Single server[/B]: just put the jar on your Spigot / Paper server.
[*][B]BungeeCord or Velocity[/B]: put the jar on your proxy, it runs the bot. Roles follow the permissions the player has on the proxy.
[*][B]PlaceholderAPI behind a proxy[/B]: also put the jar on your Spigot servers with [I]standalone: true[/I]. They don't start the bot and receive the data from the proxy (plugin messages, or Redis with [I]redis.enable: true[/I]).
[*][B]Several proxies[/B]: with RedisBungee, one proxy runs the bot and another one takes over automatically if it goes down.
[*][B]Commands on your Spigot servers[/B]: prefix a link or boost reward command with [I][FORWARD] [/I] to run it on the Spigot servers connected to Redis instead of the proxy. It needs Redis and the same [I]redis.secret[/I] (a long random value) on the proxy and on every Spigot server.
[/LIST]

[IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Benoit-V/DiscordRankSync/master/docs/spigot/header-config.png[/IMG]

Every option is documented in the default [URL='https://github.com/Benoit-V/DiscordRankSync/blob/master/Common/src/main/resources/config.yml']config.yml[/URL]: ranks, rewards, boost delay, join message for unlinked players, bot activity, databases, Redis and all the messages.

